            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for to host, then the Tamil for a farewell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: முதுமை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "முதுமை — mutumai — \"old age\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "முதுமையில் தனிமை ஒரு பெரிய பிரச்சினை. mutumaiyil taṉimai oru periya piracciṉai. Loneliness is a big problem in old age."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From முது \"old\"; முதுமையில், in old age."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "முதுமை (mutumai) is native Dravidian (DEDR 4954), the noun of முது mutu, \"old, ancient\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
